## Section 6 — Competitive White Space (What Competitors Are Missing)

Major portals (Poki, CrazyGames, Y8) leave critical gaps that PlayThorn can exploit:

1. **Ad-Free Self-Hosted Open Source Corner**: Poki & CrazyGames force 30-second unskippable video ads before every game session. By self-hosting MIT/CC0 open-source WebGL games (e.g. *HexGL*, *BrowserQuest*, *OpenRA*, *Hextris*), PlayThorn can market **"Instant 0-Ad Web Gaming"**.
2. **Indie WebGPU & Shader Showcase**: Competitors ignore experimental WebGPU titles. PlayThorn can introduce a dedicated **"WebGPU Next-Gen"** category to attract early-adopter tech enthusiasts.
3. **Curated Progressive Web App (PWA) Offline Play**: Competitors require a constant live internet connection. PlayThorn can allow self-hosted WASM games to be saved to IndexedDB for **offline browser play on mobile devices**.

