├─ Week 2: Integrate 10 Additional WASM/3D Repos (OpenRA, Clumsy Bird 3D, MineClone, Space Company, TrackMania Web)
├─ Week 3: Upgrade Next.js Container with SharedArrayBuffer & Cross-Origin Isolation headers
└─ Week 4: QA testing, mobile touch controls verification, IndexedDB offline caching setup

MONTH 2: Commercial & Publisher Licensing (100 Games)
├─ Week 5-6: Purchase 25 Commercial Source Codes from CodeCanyon & Scirra Store
├─ Week 7-8: Sign B2B Agreements with Famobi & Softgames for 75 Premium Casual/Puzzle Titles

MONTH 3: Scale to 500+ & Indie Developer Portal (500+ Games)
├─ Week 9-10: Launch PlayThorn Developer Rev-Share Submission Portal for itch.io creators
├─ Week 11-12: Curate top 10% of GameDistribution B2B catalog to reach 500+ high-craft games
```

---

## Section 14 — Brutally Honest Risks & Technical Unknowns

1. **Copyright Risk on Viral Web Games**: Popular games like *Eaglercraft* (Minecraft web port) carry **high legal risk (RED)** and should be strictly excluded despite high user demand.
2. **Unity WebGL RAM Overhead on Low-End Mobile**: Large Unity WebGL builds (30MB+) will crash on older mobile devices with <2GB RAM. PlayCanvas and Phaser 3 must be prioritized for mobile users.
3. **SharedArrayBuffer Header Side-Effects**: Enabling `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` on Next.js can block third-party iframe embeds unless served from credentialless origins.

